A||||6||88 Database Nut||Junkyard Dogs and '88 Fieros||||7||
Z||000000||88 Database Nut||01-19-2000||08:06 AM||||Hey guys, I remember in the old days that most junkyards always had a couple of beasties around for the late shift.  I've been to alot of yards up here in GA (some very rural) but haven't even seen signs warning about dogs, let alone a dog. Has this gone by the wayside with modern surveillance tech where y'all are?<P>Seperate comment:  If you see an '88 at a junkyard, PLEASE get the vin for me for the '88 Database Project I'm running.  We have 923 cars documented now, but I really hate to read stories like fierodave's where the car gets crushed and no one will ever know what the VIN was. Ray Paulk is doing the 84-87, and '88 ttops databases, so VINs for those years can be sent to him.  You can see a summary of the '88 Database Cars at:  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/motorcity/track/3487" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/motorcity/track/3487</A>  .||||reg||7
Z||000001||Deer_Slayer||01-19-2000||08:37 AM||||The one yard I went to still had dogs, but they were not the beastly kind.  Instead, there was a bunch of poodles and a cocker spaniel that just layed in the sun.  At least, the guy at the yard said, they help in keeping the snakes out. ||||reg||6
Z||000002||Raydar||01-19-2000||11:05 AM||||Poodles?!?! HAHAHAHAHAH!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||01-19-2000||11:39 AM||||one of the yards here, has a couple of dogs on chains.  but they are all big pets, wanting attention, nudging into you so you have to pet them... i'm so scarred!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||01-19-2000||12:32 PM||||Don's in Augusta, GA has a large German Shepherd in a fenced in dog run near the entrance.  He is usually pretty annoyed at people coming and going.  i wouldn't want to venture into the yard after hours.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||01-19-2000||01:35 PM||||Some of the yards around here don't even have gates to close at night! ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||01-19-2000||05:43 PM||||We have a boneyard around here that has all of the fancy, high-tech stuff.  Electric fence, video cameras (4 at last count!), "professional" guard dogs, and occasional security cops!  This is a nice, well equipped yard, but maybe this is going too far!  (On the other hand, maybe this is to protect something other than rusting cars.  Hint, hint!)  I guess this is why they want $150 for a Vista Vent!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
